Issue #1696 attribution proof, captured 2026-09-02T16:16:48Z

Substrate. A throwaway Postgres with all 132 migrations applied by
scripts/ci-throwaway-db.sh from supabase/migrations, so the catalog and the
ledger schema are the real ones. control-plane and edge-api are built from
source: edge-api twice, once from origin/main (the BEFORE binary) and once
from this branch (the AFTER binary), both against the same database. Two
stand-ins and only two: a LiteLLM that answers /v1/embeddings with
prompt_tokens 1500, and an HTTPS JWKS the real Supabase validator fetches
and verifies. Nothing about attribution is stubbed.

Fixture. Two funded, billable tenants: the searching customer and a separate
platform account that owns OWUI_SHIM_KEY, each granted 1,000,000,000 credits
(1 USD at the D-046 peg). The searching user's JWT deliberately carries NO
tenant_id claim, which is the shape Open WebUI's SSO tokens actually have,
so the tenant is resolved through the real OWUI-scoped tenant fallback.

Price. hive-embedding-default, catalog input price 10,000 credits per
million tokens, read from public.model_aliases by the migration chain. 1500
tokens is therefore exactly 15 credits, and 15 is what every leg below is
checked against.

Balances are read straight out of public.credit_ledger_entries with the same
SQL apps/control-plane/internal/ledger/repository.go GetBalance runs.

=== 0. baseline ===
     label      | posted_credits | reserved_credits 
----------------+----------------+------------------
 searching user |      999999970 |                0
 OWUI shim      |      999999985 |                0
(2 rows)


=== 1. BEFORE, edge-api built from origin/main ===
POST /v1/embeddings with Authorization: Bearer <OWUI_SHIM_KEY> and no carrier
header, which is byte for byte what the chat container sends today.
HTTP 200
     label      | posted_credits | reserved_credits 
----------------+----------------+------------------
 searching user |      999999970 |                0
 OWUI shim      |      999999970 |                0
(2 rows)

Verdict: served, and the 15 credits came off the PLATFORM account. The
customer who searched is untouched. That is issue #1696.

=== 2. AFTER, edge-api built from this branch, same request, still no carrier ===
HTTP 401
     label      | posted_credits | reserved_credits 
----------------+----------------+------------------
 searching user |      999999970 |                0
 OWUI shim      |      999999970 |                0
(2 rows)

Verdict: refused. Neither balance moves, so there is no fallback to the
platform account left on this path.

=== 3. AFTER, the request the patched chat container sends ===
Authorization: Bearer <OWUI_SHIM_KEY> plus X-Hive-Upstream-Auth carrying the
searching user's own token.
HTTP 200
     label      | posted_credits | reserved_credits 
----------------+----------------+------------------
 searching user |      999999955 |                0
 OWUI shim      |      999999970 |                0
(2 rows)

Verdict: served, and the 15 credits came off the SEARCHING CUSTOMER. The
platform account is exactly where leg 1 left it.

